<title>HONG KONG: People's Bank of China mandates US$100 mln loan.</title>
<headline>People's Bank of China mandates US$100 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The People's Bank of China has mandated HongKong Bank China Services and DKB Hong Kong to arrange a US$100 million loan facility, bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the amortising loan has a final maturity of 15 years.</p>
<p>Repayment is in equal semi-annual instalments after a grace period of four years.</p>
<p>Pricing is not available yet.</p>
<p>Proceeds are to be used for a new power plant in China's central Henan province.</p>
<p>The deal has been fully underwritten.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
